From 863cf8ab7fc151388bf1f30d2a7324025ea09153 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Van Tran <trantoanvan@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:24:49 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(inbox): "Needs you" and "For your info" tabs

The active inbox shows one of two tabs. "Needs you" holds the items the
server already marks above info (action_required: assigned to you, a
decision to answer, a run that failed; attention: an autopilot problem);
"For your info" holds the rest. It opens on "Needs you" while that holds
anything; the count there is red. Each "Needs you" row starts with a chip
naming why (its kind). Archive stays "Done"; filters apply inside the tab.
Web only: severity is already on every item. Reference: OpenMausBot's
Needs you / For your info / Done.

Patch-Id: inbox-split
